      "description": "Watch Sweden vs Romania highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 25, 2026. The UEFA Nations League delivered another high-stakes encounter as two ambitious sides clashed in a match defined by tactical discipline and moments of individual brilliance. With both teams eager to claim dominance, the atmosphere was electric from the very first whistle. A First-Half Goal Fest On 2026-09-25 , the game burst into life in the 20th minute when Sweden broke the deadlock. Yasin Ayari turned provider, setting up Alexander Isak , who clinically finished with his right foot to give the hosts the lead. However, Romania refused to back down. In the 29th minute, Andrei Ratiu delivered a precise ball to Dennis Man , who leveled the scores with a composed left-footed strike, momentarily silencing the 31,882 fans in attendance. As the first half drew to a close, Sweden regained their advantage through a moment of magic. In the 43rd minute, Lucas Bergvall found Viktor Gyoekeres , who unleashed a stunning volley into the back of the net. The clinical finish ensured the Swedish side went into the break with their noses in front after an exhausting opening period. VAR Drama and Defensive Resilience The second half was heavily influenced by the Video Assistant Referee. Sweden thought they had extended their lead in the 54th minute, but after a lengthy VAR review, the goal was revoked due to a foul committed earlier in the build-up. This reprieve gave Romania a lifeline, but they struggled to break down a resolute Swedish defense anchored by Victor Lindelof . In the closing stages, the match became increasingly physical as Romania desperately chased an equalizer. Vladimir Screciu , Dennis Man , and Andrei Coubis all saw yellow cards for tactical fouls and dangerous challenges. Despite several tactical substitutions and late pressure from the visitors, Sweden maintained 60% possession and navigated the final minutes successfully to secure a well-deserved victory."
